ing* true]\\n  2469\\t       (annotate-call-sites (compile-form-1 form tail? env macro-env))))))\\n  2470\\t\\n  2471\\t\\n  2472\\t(defn- top-level-defined-fns\\n  2473\\t  \\\"Plain symbols in `forms` whose top-level definitions are exclusively native\\n  2474\\t   `defn` or `defn-` descriptors. Any `def`, `defmacro`, or external macro\\n  2475\\t   excludes the symbol (or the unit, when macros are active) from static\\n  2476\\t   intra-unit dispatch so dynamic admission still governs.\\\"\\n  2477\\t  [forms external-macros]\\n  2478\\t  (if (or (seq external-macros)\\n  2479\\t          (some #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmacro (first %))) forms))\\n  2480\\t    #{}\\n  2481\\t    (:fns\\n  2482\\t      (reduce (fn [{:keys [fns non-fns] :as acc} f]\\n  2483\\t                (if-not (and (seq? f) (symbol? (second f)))\\n  2484\\t                  acc\\n  2485\\t                  (let [head (first f)\\n  2486\\t                        sym  (strip-symbol-meta (second f))]\\n  2487\\t                    (cond\\n  2488\\t                      (= 'def head)\\n  2489\\t                      {:fns (disj fns sym), :non-fns (conj non-fns sym)}\\n  2490\\t\\n  2491\\t                      (contains? #{'defn 'defn-} head)\\n  2492\\t                      {:fns     (if (contains? non-fns sym) fns (conj fns sym))\\n  2493\\t                       :non-fns non-fns}\\n  2494\\t\\n  2495\\t                      :else acc))))\\n  2496\\t              {:fns #{}, :non-fns #{}}\\n  2497\\t              forms))))\\n  2498\\t\\n  2499\\t\\n  2500\\t(defn- program-env\\n  2501\\t  \\\"The compile-time env of one program. Without `opts` it is empty: the\\n  2502\\t   native path. `{:convention :arg-vector, :native #{symbol}, :macros\\n  2503\\t   #{symbol}}` opts into the argument-vector convention: `:native` names the\\n  2504\\t   primitives a bare symbol may call directly (a set, or a map from name to\\n  2505\\t   its published profile, whose `:yin.k/arities` give an adapter its admitted\